  "root_review": {
    "record": "docs/handoffs/reader-next-wave/J06-ROOT-REVIEW.md at 2b1ca2d1",
    "findings": [
      "external() validated everything after the scheme with the query rules, so %0A/%0D/%7F in an authority, path or fragment still became NEEDS_HOST",
      "internal() checked fragment hex and controls but never decoded the escapes, so #a%FF entered INTERNAL instead of BAD_ESCAPE"
    ],
    "fix": "escapes are now validated per URI component: query data (before any fragment) may carry encoded C0/DEL bytes, authority/path/fragment may not; fragments decode through the same UTF-8 state machine as container paths and report BAD_ESCAPE for invalid, truncated or overlong sequences. The public header comment, the contract document and the fixture table were updated together; no URL or book parser was added and the SDK/schema/hosts are untouched."
  },
